before:
Worked example:

```javascript
function logSummary(event) {
  return {requestId:event.requestId,status:event.status};
}
console.log(logSummary({"requestId":"r1","status":500,"token":"secret","body":"private"}));
```
The returned value is {"requestId":"r1","status":500}.

after:
This event also contains private fields. The summary leaves them out.

```javascript
function logSummary(event) {
  return {requestId:event.requestId,status:event.status};
}
console.log(logSummary({"requestId":"r1","status":500,"token":"secret","body":"private"}));
```

The result is {requestId:"r1", status:500}. It has no token or body field.
